// IRIW with an SC fence between each reader's two relaxed loads.
//
// rmm-zoo property: mca (Atomicity), and the C++20-vs-C11 ordering edge.
// Source: Batty, Donaldson & Wickerson, "Overhauling SC Atomics in C11 and
//         OpenCL" (POPL 2016); Lahav et al., "Repairing Sequential Consistency
//         in C/C++11" (PLDI 2017); Boehm, Giroux & Vafeiadis, P0668R5 (2018).
//         Vendored shape: rmm-zoo litmus/incomparable/C++20-vs-C11/IRIW+scfences.
//
// C++11/14/17 seq_cst FENCES are too weak to forbid this -- a known defect.
// C++20 adopted the repaired seq_cst of P0668 (the RC11 fragment), which forbids
// it. A multicopy-atomic model forbids it outright.
//
// Reference verdicts: C11 / C++17 ALLOW (the defect).
//                     RC11 / C++20 / SC FORBID.
x := 0;
y := 0;
{
  x :rlx= 1
} ||| {
  y :rlx= 1
} ||| {
  r1 :rlx= x;
  fence(sc);
  r2 :rlx= y
} ||| {
  r3 :rlx= y;
  fence(sc);
  r4 :rlx= x
}
%%
allow (r1 = 1 && r2 = 0 && r3 = 1 && r4 = 0) [C11]
